      "Language": "eng",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "This article recounts the experience of an 88-year-old woman with sciatic pain and her attempts to get it treated. Common interventions were utilized and failed, and back surgery was recommended. A patient advocate was consulted who suggested the need to begin to exercise and to reconsider other medical interventions. Within 2 months, she was pain-free and returned to her active lifestyle. The use of scientific evidence and common sense prevented unnecessary surgery and other costly medical treatments."},
